export anchor Product:
    name: NameTempest
    site: nametempest.com
    summary:
        A web application and paid service. A person works in a browser and
        installs nothing.
    purpose:
        NameTempest helps a person find a good company name. The person
        describes the company in plain words. The application uses a large
        language model to suggest names, revises them over several rounds,
        and checks whether a name has a free .com domain.

        Naming a company is slow work. A person can usually say what the
        company does, but producing many plausible names, judging them, and
        checking domains by hand takes hours and often ends in a name
        nobody is happy with.
    promise:
        The person leaves with a shortlist of names they would accept, and
        knows which of those names have a free .com domain.
    nameRule:
        The product name is NameTempest. The site is nametempest.com.
        Every customer-facing text uses one of these two forms and never a
        third spelling.

export anchor Audiences:
    dayOne:
        The first version serves all three groups below at the same time.
        They share one flow. They differ in what they write in the company
        description and in the style options they pick, not in the
        features they get.
    segments:
        - Solo founders and small startup teams naming a new company
        - Small-business owners naming a shop, studio or service
        - Branding and marketing agencies naming for several clients
    sharedNeeds:
        - Many plausible names in a short time
        - Help judging which names are good and which sound wrong
        - Certainty about whether a name can be used on the web
    agencyNeed:
        An agency names for several clients. One browser must be able to
        hold more than one naming project, and no name or note from one
        project may appear in another. An agency with three or more people
        works in a Studio organization, where projects are shared between
        members.

export anchor Scope:
    included:
        - Describe a company and generate names with an AI model
        - Refine a candidate list over revision rounds
        - Pick an effort level for a round, which selects the model that does the work
        - Check .com domain availability for one name or a whole shortlist
        - Keep a shortlist, compare names, and drop names the person rejects
        - Shape the style of a round with one short form
        - Copy or download a shortlist
        - Take a project out as a file, and delete a project or an account
        - Work without an account up to a free allowance
        - Sign in with an email address and a password, or an email magic link
        - Buy a monthly plan, Pro or Studio, and optional credit top-ups
        - Run a Studio organization with at least three seats, shared projects and an owner
        - Edit a shared Studio project together, with each member's changes appearing live
        - Run an operator admin interface that sets every limit and price, chooses the model for each effort level, and fixes a person's account, plan, credits and seats
        - See a plain message and one retry when something fails, and report a repeated failure to the operator
    excluded:
        - Registering domains or sending the person to a registrar to buy one
        - Trademark searches or legal clearance
        - Company registration with any authority
        - Logo design, brand identity, or written brand guidelines
        - Social handle availability checks
        - Sharing a project on the Pro plan, which serves one person
        - A second organization role beyond owner and member
        - A public gallery of generated names
        - Native mobile applications
        - Top-level domains other than .com
        - Taking payments, issuing refunds or changing a bill inside the admin interface
    later:
        - Social handle checks
        - Trademark screening
        - Roles beyond owner and member, such as an admin
        - A choice of top-level domains
    reasonForExclusions:
        Each item in the later list adds a paid outside service or a large
        new surface. The first version keeps only the one check that
        decides whether a name can be used on the web today.

export anchor SuccessCriteria:
    fullSessionWithoutAccount:
        A first-time visitor with no account can describe a company,
        generate names, revise once, check the domains of a shortlist, and
        copy the shortlist away.
    honestAvailability:
        No name is ever shown as available unless a fresh live check
        confirmed it for that name. A failed check, a doubtful reply or a
        disputed answer is shown as unknown, never as available. A name
        that cannot form a valid .com domain is shown as not valid, with
        the reason in plain words, and spends no check.
    gateKeepsWork:
        When the free allowance runs out, every name and note already on
        screen stays on screen. The person loses nothing and sees the ways
        to continue.
    separateProjects:
        Two naming projects in the same browser never share names, notes
        or check results.
    studioSeats:
        A studio with three seats can invite two people, who each sign in
        with an email address and a password or a magic link, and work on
        the same shared project at the same time without overwriting each
        other.
    liveTogether:
        Two members of an organization with the same shared project open see
        each other's added names appear without refreshing the page.
    resetIsSlow:
        Clearing the browser gives one fresh free allowance and no more.
        Using up the free use from one network address stops further free
        rounds from that address for the month, while signing in with an
        account that has allowance always continues the work.
    workLeaves:
        A person can export a project as a file and can delete a project or
        an account at any time without asking support. A deleted account
        restores in full for 30 days and is gone after that.
    honestFailure:
        When the model, the lookup or a payment fails, the person sees a
        plain message and one retry, and nothing that failed is charged.
        The same part failing again reaches the operator without the person
        writing to support.
    verifiable:
        Every requirement here can be checked by using the site in a
        browser, with no access to the inside of the system.

export anchor MonthGoals:
    base:
        The first month succeeds when every behaviour requirement above
        holds in the shipped product and every failure that repeats reaches
        the operator. No further behaviour goal is added for the first
        month.
    numbers:
        Three numbers are set by the operator before launch, and the first
        month is judged against them: paying people, free-to-paid
        conversion, and names kept in a shortlist.
    payingPeople:
        How many people pay for a plan by the end of the first month. The
        operator decides before launch whether one Studio organization
        counts as one paying customer or as one per seat, and writes that
        choice down with the number.
    conversion:
        Of the people who used the free allowance and did not pay, the share
        who then buy a plan. The operator sets the number before launch.
    shortlist:
        The typical number of names a person keeps in a shortlist on one
        project. The operator sets the number before launch. This is the
        sign that the names are good enough to use, not only to read.
    why:
        The three numbers test whether the product is useful, not only
        working: someone pays, a free visitor turns into a paying one, and
        the names survive a person's own judgement.
    counted:
        Each number is counted from the product's own records: accounts and
        plans for payers, the counters of a device or account for
        conversion, and saved shortlists for the last one.
    notSettings:
        The three numbers never change what a person sees. No limit, price
        or message depends on them, and missing a number is not a failure of
        the product in front of a customer.
    out:
        Revenue totals, download counts and marketing reach are not goals of
        the first version. The first month proves the product works and that
        people want it, and is not a growth test.

export anchor Speed:
    firstNames:
        After a person submits a description, the first names appear within
        about 10 seconds. Showing them one at a time, as the model produces
        them, counts as meeting this.
    fullRound:
        A 12-name round at the default effort level finishes within about
        30 seconds. A higher level may take longer, and the person sees how
        long it is expected to take before the round starts.
    concurrency:
        The first version must serve 20 people generating names at the same
        time without any of them waiting beyond these times.
    beyondCapacity:
        Past that many at once, a person waits in a queue and sees their
        place in it. A round is never dropped without telling the person,
        and a round that never starts is never counted against the
        allowance.
    slowRound:
        A round that runs past its stated time keeps showing progress, and
        the person may cancel it. A cancelled round spends nothing, and one
        that produced nothing spends nothing.
    wording:
        These are targets measured on the shipped setup, not a contract
        with a penalty. They are part of the specification and not
        settings, so the operator cannot quietly lower them.
